ng","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MmXDbXI6Sqk"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Planned Woodstock 50 Performance","body":"Miley Cyrus was among the 80 artists originally confirmed to perform at the Woodstock 50 festival, planned for August 2019. Her inclusion was part of a diverse lineup intended to attract a wide audience for the 50th anniversary celebration, though the event was ultimately canceled. \"80 artists had originally signed up, including Santana, Dead & Company, The Killers, Jay-Z, Imagine Dragons, Cage the Elf and Miley Cyrus, Vampire Weekend, and more.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 100 Greatest Rock Moments of the Millennium So Far - Part 5: (60-51)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uEe_HLUay5M"}]}],"awards":[{"kind":"award","title":"Time 100 (2014)","body":"Won.","year":2014,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q604370"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"Disney Legends (2024)","body":"Won.","year":2024,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1150306"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"Grammy Award for Best Pop Solo Performance (2024)","body":"Won.","year":2024,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5593866"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"Grammy Award for Record of the Year (2024)","body":"Won.","year":2024,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q843219"}]}],"concerts":[{"kind":"concert","title":"Woodstock 50 (originally slated for 2019, but canceled)","body":null,"year":2019,"extra":null,"srcs":[]}],"xref":[{"kind":"xref","title":"Nine (2019) – Eighth Studio Album","body":null,"year":2019,"extra":{"from":"blink‐182","from_id":214386792607367,"type":"album"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Catching Up with Blink 182","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EaGUC4av1R4"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Musical Parent","body":"Billy Ray Cyrus is mentioned as the musical father of Miley Cyrus. \"Miley Cyrus and her dad Billy Ray.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Billy Ray Cyrus","from_id":153218094122684,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Musical Offspring","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MmXDbXI6Sqk"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Planned Woodstock 50 Performance","body":"Santana was among the 80 artists originally confirmed to perform at the Woodstock 50 festival, which was planned for August 2019 to commemorate the original event. However, the festival was ultimately canceled due to numerous logistical and financial issues. \"80 artists had originally signed up, including Santana, Dead & Company, The Killers, Jay-Z, Imagine Dragons, Cage the Elf and Miley Cyrus, Vampire Weekend, and more.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Santana","from_id":140956251051868,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 100 Greatest Rock Moments of the Millennium So Far - Part 5: (60-51)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uEe_HLUay5M"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Planned Woodstock 50 Performance","body":"Dead & Company were listed as one of the 80 artists initially scheduled to perform at the ill-fated Woodstock 50 festival in August 2019. Their participation was part of the attempt to create a diverse and commemorative lineup for the 50th anniversary of the legendary event. \"80 artists had originally signed up, including Santana, Dead & Company, The Killers, Jay-Z, Imagine Dragons, Cage the Elf and Miley Cyrus, Vampire Weekend, and more.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Dead & Company","from_id":258334026131313,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 100 Greatest Rock Moments of the Millennium So Far - Part 5: (60-51)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uEe_HLUay5M"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Planned Woodstock 50 Performance","body":"The Killers were among the 80 artists announced to perform at the Woodstock 50 festival, which aimed to celebrate the 50th anniversary of Woodstock in August 2019. Despite the star-studded lineup, the festival was eventually canceled. \"80 artists had originally signed up, including Santana, Dead & Company, The Killers, Jay-Z, Imagine Dragons, Cage the Elf and Miley Cyrus, Vampire Weekend, and more.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"The Killers","from_id":117022485418313,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 100 Greatest Rock Moments of the Millennium So Far - Part 5: (60-51)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uEe_HLUay5M"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Planned Woodstock 50 Performance","body":"Jay-Z was included in the extensive lineup of 80 artists initially committed to perform at the Woodstock 50 festival in August 2019. His planned participation highlighted the festival's ambition to draw a broad audience with a diverse array of musical acts. \"80 artists had originally signed up, including Santana, Dead & Company, The Killers, Jay-Z, Imagine Dragons, Cage the Elf and Miley Cyrus, Vampire Weekend, and more.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Jay-Z","from_id":61225788046317,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 100 Greatest Rock Moments of the Millennium So Far - Part 5: (60-51)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uEe_HLUay5M"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Planned Woodstock 50 Performance","body":"Imagine Dragons were among the 80 artists who had signed up to perform at the Woodstock 50 festival, intended to mark the 50th anniversary of the iconic 1969 event in August 2019. The festival, however, never came to fruition. \"80 artists had originally signed up, including Santana, Dead & Company, The Killers, Jay-Z, Imagine Dragons, Cage the Elf and Miley Cyrus, Vampire Weekend, and more.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Imagine Dragons","from_id":192536696866248,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 100 Greatest Rock Moments of the Millennium So Far - Part 5: (60-51)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uEe_HLUay5M"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Planned Woodstock 50 Performance","body":"Cage the Elephant was part of the original lineup of 80 artists slated to perform at the Woodstock 50 festival in August 2019, which aimed to commemorate the 50th anniversary of the legendary Woodstock event. The festival was ultimately canceled due to a host of unresolved issues. \"80 artists had originally signed up, including Santana, Dead & Company, The Killers, Jay-Z, Imagine Dragons, Cage the Elf and Miley Cyrus, Vampire Weekend, and more.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Cage the Elephant","from_id":6024924170617,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 100 Greatest Rock Moments of the Millennium So Far - Part 5: (60-51)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uEe_HLUay5M"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Planned Woodstock 50 Performance","body":"Vampire Weekend was among the 80 artists who initially committed to perform at the Woodstock 50 festival, an event planned for August 2019 to celebrate the 50th anniversary of Woodstock. The festival faced numerous problems and was eventually canceled before it could take place. \"80 artists had originally signed up, including Santana, Dead & Company, The Killers, Jay-Z, Imagine Dragons, Cage the Elf and Miley Cyrus, Vampire Weekend, and more.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Vampire Weekend","from_id":195066070988046,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 100 Greatest Rock Moments of the Millennium So Far - Part 5: (60-51)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uEe_HLUay5M"}]}],"charts":[{"id":144437294084667,"type":"album","name":"Breakout","list_id":137828800833770,"list":"RYM Top — Pop — Teen Pop","src":"musth